      "writtenOn": "2025-05-08T16:56:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This isn\u0027t safe if the host is using SME. At this point the CPU may have `SVCR.{SM,ZA}!\u003d{0,0}`, and due to preemption that may be state from a task other than `current`.\n\nBeing in that state will cause `handle___kvm_vcpu_run()` to bail out when it checks SVCR:\n\n```\n/*\n * KVM (and pKVM) doesn\u0027t support SME guests for now, and\n * ensures that SME features aren\u0027t enabled in pstate when\n * loading a vcpu. Therefore, if SME features enabled the host\n * is misbehaving.\n */\nif (unlikely(system_supports_sme() \u0026\u0026 read_sysreg_s(SYS_SVCR)))\n        goto out;\n``\n\n\nWe might be able to check SVCR here, and only save the state when that\u0027s non-zero, but I\u0027m not immediately sure if that\u0027s sufficient, or if we need to also mess with `fp_owner`, as described in the other comment below.\n\nsuspect that may lead to other problems -- see below comment about `fp_owner`.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 57,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 60,
        "endChar": 2
      },
      "revId": "1e233b959e2ceeb4ef00d1d1a310706828510f63",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
